            <ArticleTitle>Minimally Invasive Therapy for Upper Tract Urothelial Cell Cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>238-245</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1089/end.2016.0475</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Minimally invasive therapy for upper tract urothelial cell cancer has assumed an important role in the management of this relatively uncommon genitourinary malignancy. In this review, current standards for patient selection, surgical approach, as well as overall outcomes will be discussed. Moreover, the use of intraluminal agents in upper tract disease is examined along with its efficacy and associated complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
